From 2b94ff749a5e85be21d9a28f98ddaadbc616f502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:54:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a far-hold reroute never names a peer this
 host cannot serve

#3301 rebased onto ed899d12ff (#3362, the resolver's far-hold reroute) went
red: with Codex and Claude both held 9 h, kanban_paced_reroute moved a
default route to Grok (xai-oauth) even on a host with no xai-oauth
credential, so the card launched on a provider it cannot authenticate. The
governor's own pace alternate already requires live_pool_serving; the
resolver's move did not.

Rule: kanban_paced_reroute._probe takes a peer only when
kanban_provider_walls.live_pool_serving(provider, model) holds; a refused
peer is excluded and the next one probed (bounded), else the route stays
and the governor holds the card as before.

Tests: test_kanban_pace_reroute judges the governor's claim-time move with
the resolver move disabled (reroute_after_s huge) and adds two
resolver-first composition tests (far-held default card starts on Grok with
default+paced:openai-codex; with no Grok credential it stays held and
pickup_hold names the Codex hold). test_kanban_model_tier_paced_reroute
stubs live serving and adds test_a_peer_with_no_live_pool_on_this_host_is_skipped
(default / pinned / review). The 4 new tests fail without the fix; 49
importer files (973 tests) pass with it.

Task: t_d943a79dd2b3889f
